{"sha":"7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","node_id":"C_kwDOPuAjtNoAKDcwOTBmMzg2ZmJhMDBiNDdiNTgwYzE4MmYzZmRkOTM0MjI1ZjZmNTM","commit":{"author":{"name":"Jonah Gray","email":"jonah@omninode.ai","date":"2026-08-28T20:13:12Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-08-28T20:13:12Z"},"message":"fix(OMN-16493): fence node_projection_delegation 0031 so its abort stops blocking the BYOK migrations (#2974)\n\nOperator ruling 2026-08-28, verbatim: \"Fence 0031, HOLD the repin\".\n\n0031's ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE UUID USING (CASE ... END) has no ELSE branch, so\nthe 9 live rows under 5 slugs outside its closed map convert to NULL and trip\nthe pre-existing NOT NULL from 0022. The migration aborts, and because both\nrunners are set -e / ON_ERROR_STOP=1 and iterate node dirs LC_ALL=C-sorted,\nthat abort killed the whole Job before node_projection_tenant_credentials'\n0001/0002 were ever attempted -- blocking a beta-critical BYOK lane on a\ntenancy ruling it has nothing to do with, purely by lexical sort order.\n\nFencing lets the loop continue (the fenced-id skip runs ahead of the ledger\nprobe). It does not fix 0031, and it is not a workaround for a defect in it:\n0031's guard is firing as designed, the map is incomplete by construction\nbecause the writer keeps minting new slugs (OMN-16804), and 0031 cannot be\nedited in place (already applied on the .201 dev lane -- conflicting migration\nchecksum, the OMN-16705 class).\n\nKnowingly deferred: 0031 stays unapplied, so OMN-15683's UUID-key defect stays\nlive and OMN-16493 stays open.","tree":{"sha":"10c66cf6efcd18eda8aa5b8ece260ff6bb89bdea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/trees/10c66cf6efcd18eda8aa5b8ece260ff6bb89bdea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/git/commits/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkevYCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAHBgQAIjHRwlOSjgXRq4qyWFGQH3I\nqcinTbIChpglDz3bUbDIMxqsSO0xriMEOYlTb0Xiyd/X5C5l9Q0wMGmgINHyckBd\ntiXLavEwsMI/HJEfXhzjEEtWw3DDWEthqyC9BNYw/yPm/g1LiZ6pDfovWl5xDpzK\nXYNr6HZfC5e//NpgdwPBEhDOe5bp1+BXQEcT5Nwj7crZNRbM2TW1Wk6hUEs2HzgH\nSlLa7Qp/igT0Y2Fesd+9KELZJTNyF0IN3sawlNSeUYQnNyqgbEV7YjPbEBb7FT/9\nooEVkwwuo/Dx34Y4OqwckIx9qOnirXRGMvoj2px+AUYxY9sReB0rkmWL8Rx6BJed\n3yQt+nW6I4XYQexAskr7jwEjmr7yyCRy8AASYs++lnYyHVIXl+6bc54AMoTj2+nB\n8sD+wvX8ZU3hvy5NUL+83fJLCvU0+/rZotci5G6rArwQpra//vJP8VqLvOmCmiGJ\n9HL+0CIkGLubwDBbwGyeoy4LMd3tXRpEf6wcNxlTi72yr4P4PS0vUQisyT4/cSUE\nCKpDrhs2TDaDp0bPMF5A8PSkARYalxxH15fSCaaGO/yEvYIA0Nnueu+y8b1a4bSY\nRlz7eJWXTTxKAlK/UpVYFtEftQ4QhS3FzY6We3xDtcR5tREd/DrsrvTUzGAhW6wX\nI4yKV27eLSd3iquSsz3B\n=TL9p\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 10c66cf6efcd18eda8aa5b8ece260ff6bb89bdea\nparent 960255103ae08b883f0f3d04e2c051b5de6e0d00\nauthor Jonah Gray <jonah@omninode.ai> 1787947992 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787947992 +0000\n\nfix(OMN-16493): fence node_projection_delegation 0031 so its abort stops blocking the BYOK migrations (#2974)\n\nOperator ruling 2026-08-28, verbatim: \"Fence 0031, HOLD the repin\".\n\n0031's ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE UUID USING (CASE ... END) has no ELSE branch, so\nthe 9 live rows under 5 slugs outside its closed map convert to NULL and trip\nthe pre-existing NOT NULL from 0022. The migration aborts, and because both\nrunners are set -e / ON_ERROR_STOP=1 and iterate node dirs LC_ALL=C-sorted,\nthat abort killed the whole Job before node_projection_tenant_credentials'\n0001/0002 were ever attempted -- blocking a beta-critical BYOK lane on a\ntenancy ruling it has nothing to do with, purely by lexical sort order.\n\nFencing lets the loop continue (the fenced-id skip runs ahead of the ledger\nprobe). It does not fix 0031, and it is not a workaround for a defect in it:\n0031's guard is firing as designed, the map is incomplete by construction\nbecause the writer keeps minting new slugs (OMN-16804), and 0031 cannot be\nedited in place (already applied on the .201 dev lane -- conflicting migration\nchecksum, the OMN-16705 class).\n\nKnowingly deferred: 0031 stays unapplied, so OMN-15683's UUID-key defect stays\nlive and OMN-16493 stays open.","verified_at":"2026-08-28T20:13:12Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53/comments","author":{"login":"jonahgabriel","id":1002253,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDIyNTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1002253?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel","html_url":"https://github.com/jonahgabriel","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonahgabriel/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"committer":{"login":"web-flow","id":19864447,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"960255103ae08b883f0f3d04e2c051b5de6e0d00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commits/960255103ae08b883f0f3d04e2c051b5de6e0d00","html_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/commit/960255103ae08b883f0f3d04e2c051b5de6e0d00"}],"stats":{"total":102,"additions":98,"deletions":4},"files":[{"sha":"b38f84770fdca46ea81752760ef28b0ba0e188a3","filename":"docker/migrations/forward/fenced-node-migrations.yaml","status":"modified","additions":76,"deletions":2,"changes":78,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/blob/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53/docker%2Fmigrations%2Fforward%2Ffenced-node-migrations.yaml","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/raw/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53/docker%2Fmigrations%2Fforward%2Ffenced-node-migrations.yaml","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/contents/docker%2Fmigrations%2Fforward%2Ffenced-node-migrations.yaml?ref=7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","patch":"@@ -64,12 +64,14 @@\n # (e.g. widening ruling 21's scope, or adding a new ruling-15-style lane\n # carve-out) is a separate, explicit edit to that runner's release block.\n #\n-# WHY THESE TEN IDS (verbatim rationale, unchanged from the pre-OMN-15349\n+# WHY THESE ELEVEN IDS (verbatim rationale, unchanged from the pre-OMN-15349\n # hand-maintained lists for the first seven; the eighth (node_pr_review_bot\n # 001) was added under OMN-15717/OMN-15376, the ninth\n # (delegation_inference_response 0003) under OMN-15336 item 4 / OMN-15656 —\n # two independent PRs landing concurrently, both additive, not conflicting —\n-# and the tenth (hook_event_capture 0002) under OMN-16090):\n+# the tenth (hook_event_capture 0002) under OMN-16090, and the ELEVENTH\n+# (delegation 0031) under OMN-16493 / the 2026-08-28 \"Fence 0031, HOLD the\n+# repin\" operator ruling):\n #   delegation 0023-0026 — OMN-14974 / OMN-15313. Tenant-isolation RLS on\n #     live, actively-written delegation tables; un-gate only in a change that\n #     also proves the writer sets app.tenant_id per connection. No lane may\n@@ -142,6 +144,76 @@\n #     sibling stays fenced would make this the only RLS-enforcing relation on\n #     the surface, an inconsistency worth deciding deliberately rather than\n #     inheriting from whichever change happened to land last.\n+#\n+#   delegation 0031 — OMN-16493, added under the 2026-08-28 operator ruling\n+#     \"Fence 0031, HOLD the repin\" (answer to the OMN-15954 comment 85b7ccab\n+#     decision brief, §6 option A). This is the ELEVENTH id and the first one\n+#     fenced for a reason that is neither an RLS posture nor a shape gate: it\n+#     is fenced because the migration ABORTS, and its abort takes an unrelated\n+#     team's migrations down with it.\n+#\n+#     WHAT ACTUALLY FAILS. 0031 converts delegation_events.tenant_id from the\n+#     legacy TEXT slug to the canonical UUID via\n+#     `ALTER COLUMN ... TYPE UUID USING (CASE tenant_id WHEN ... END)` with no\n+#     ELSE branch. The column has been NOT NULL since 0022 (applied\n+#     2026-07-28), so any slug outside 0031's closed 3-value map evaluates to\n+#     NULL and trips that pre-existing constraint:\n+#       ERROR: column \"tenant_id\" of relation \"delegation_events\"\n+#              contains null values\n+#     Re-measured live 2026-08-28: 165 rows, 9 of them under 5 slugs the map\n+#     does not know — and one of those, `t-REDACTED-OMN17288`, is a REAL, ACTIVE,\n+#     externally-owned customer provisioned 8 days after 0031 was authored.\n+#     The data is not null; the mapping is incomplete, and it is incomplete\n+#     BY CONSTRUCTION because the writer keeps minting new slugs (OMN-16804).\n+#     That is 0031's second fail-closed guard firing exactly as designed. It\n+#     is NOT a defect in 0031 and this entry is NOT a workaround for one.\n+#\n+#     WHY 0031's OWN DIAGNOSTICS NEVER SAID SO. delegation_events carries\n+#     ENABLE+FORCE RLS with `tenant_isolation USING (tenant_id =\n+#     current_setting('app.tenant_id', true))`, and the migrate Job's identity\n+#     (role_omnidash) has rolbypassrls=f. With app.tenant_id unset the policy\n+#     matches nothing, so 0031's opening `DELETE ... WHERE correlation_id IN\n+#     (...)` is a silent zero-row no-op and its `IF EXISTS` pre-guard — the\n+#     one that would RAISE the useful \"no canonical UUID mapping for tenant\n+#     value %\" — sees nothing. Only the ALTER ... TYPE rewrite, which is not\n+#     RLS-filtered, sees the real rows. Every actionable diagnostic this\n+#     migration built for exactly this case is blinded; the uninformative\n+#     NOT-NULL error is all that survives, which is why this read as a\n+#     NULL-data problem for a week.\n+#\n+#     WHY THAT MAKES IT A FENCE AND NOT A FIX. 0031 cannot be edited in place:\n+#     it is already applied on the .201 dev compose lane, and\n+#     `_ledger/bootstrap.sql` raises `conflicting migration checksum` on any\n+#     byte change (the OMN-16705 class). The real fix is a new `0030a_`\n+#     pre-step (fully specified on OMN-16493) over a slug set that is finally\n+#     CLOSED, which needs OMN-16804 first (gateway stamps the verified UUID\n+#     rather than the slug, removing the map from the write path). Landing a\n+#     hardcoded `0030a_` map today ships something permanently immutable and\n+#     already known incomplete — and worth less every day the beta adds\n+#     tenants.\n+#\n+#     WHO WAS PAYING FOR IT. The node loop iterates node directories\n+#     LC_ALL=C-sorted; `node_projection_delegation` sorts before\n+#     `node_projection_tenant_credentials`; both runners are set -e with\n+#     `psql -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1`. So 0031's abort killed the WHOLE Job before\n+#     node_projection_tenant_credentials/0001_relax_name_provider_not_null and\n+#     0002_credential_identity_not_null were ever attempted — blocking a\n+#     beta-critical BYOK integration on a tenancy ruling it has nothing to do\n+#     with, purely by lexical sort order. The fenced-id skip runs AHEAD of the\n+#     ledger probe (run-forward-migrations.sh:1272-1289; the k8s Job's\n+#     equivalent block), so fencing lets the loop continue and those two\n+#     migrations apply on the next green deploy.\n+#\n+#     WHAT THIS FENCE KNOWINGLY COSTS, recorded so a future reader does not\n+#     re-derive it: 0031 stays unapplied, so OMN-15683's UUID-key defect stays\n+#     live — UUID-keyed dashboard reads of delegation_events keep returning\n+#     ZERO ROWS with no error for every real provisioned tenant — and\n+#     OMN-16493 stays open. That was ruled acceptable in exchange for\n+#     unblocking the BYOK lane; it is a deferral, not a resolution.\n+#\n+#     UN-GATE ONLY when OMN-16804 has removed the slug map from the write path\n+#     and a `0030a_` pre-step exists that defeats the RLS blindness described\n+#     above inside a single DO block. Do NOT un-gate by editing 0031's bytes.\n fenced_node_migrations:\n   - id: \"node:node_projection_delegation:0023_delegation_rls_tenant_isolation.sql\"\n     ticket: \"OMN-14974\"\n@@ -163,3 +235,5 @@ fenced_node_migrations:\n     ticket: \"OMN-15336\"\n   - id: \"node:node_hook_event_capture:0002_hook_events_tenant_rls.sql\"\n     ticket: \"OMN-16090\"\n+  - id: \"node:node_projection_delegation:0031_delegation_events_tenant_id_to_uuid.sql\"\n+    ticket: \"OMN-16493\""},{"sha":"faa3313facee539691220916aa09eeec6a003ee2","filename":"tests/scripts/test_node_migration_fence_parity.py","status":"modified","additions":22,"deletions":2,"changes":24,"blob_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/blob/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53/tests%2Fscripts%2Ftest_node_migration_fence_parity.py","raw_url":"https://github.com/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/raw/7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53/tests%2Fscripts%2Ftest_node_migration_fence_parity.py","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OmniNode-ai/omnibase_infra/contents/tests%2Fscripts%2Ftest_node_migration_fence_parity.py?ref=7090f386fba00b47b580c182f3fdd934225f6f53","patch":"@@ -313,6 +313,20 @@ def manifest_ids() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n FENCED_HOOK_EVENT_CAPTURE_IDS = (\n     \"node:node_hook_event_capture:0002_hook_events_tenant_rls.sql\",\n )\n+# OMN-16493, under the 2026-08-28 operator ruling \"Fence 0031, HOLD the repin\".\n+# The first id here fenced for neither an RLS posture nor a shape gate: 0031's\n+# `ALTER COLUMN tenant_id TYPE UUID USING (CASE ... END)` has no ELSE, so the 9\n+# live rows under 5 slugs outside its closed map convert to NULL and trip the\n+# pre-existing NOT NULL from 0022 -- the migration ABORTS, and because both\n+# runners are set -e / ON_ERROR_STOP=1 and iterate node dirs LC_ALL=C-sorted,\n+# that abort killed the whole Job before node_projection_tenant_credentials'\n+# 0001/0002 were ever attempted. Fencing is what decouples the BYOK lane from\n+# the tenancy ruling; the real fix is a `0030a_` pre-step after OMN-16804\n+# closes the slug set, never an edit to 0031's bytes (already applied on the\n+# .201 dev lane -- `conflicting migration checksum`, the OMN-16705 class).\n+FENCED_DELEGATION_UUID_CONVERSION_IDS = (\n+    \"node:node_projection_delegation:0031_delegation_events_tenant_id_to_uuid.sql\",\n+)\n # Pinned expectation for the manifest content (OMN-15349): the baseline fence,\n # exact and in order. A manifest edit that moves this must update the pin in\n # the same PR — same change-control friction the pre-OMN-15349 shell-literal\n@@ -323,6 +337,7 @@ def manifest_ids() -> tuple[str, ...]:\n     + FENCED_PR_REVIEW_BOT_IDS\n     + FENCED_INFERENCE_RESPONSE_IDS\n     + FENCED_HOOK_EVENT_CAPTURE_IDS\n+    + FENCED_DELEGATION_UUID_CONVERSION_IDS\n )\n \n # --- OMN-15336 item 4 repair (D1, 2026-08-05): FORCE-RLS grandfather snapshot\n@@ -615,8 +630,13 @@ def test_manifest_pins_the_known_baseline_fence() -> None:\n     assert (\n         found[pr_review_bot_end:inference_response_end] == FENCED_INFERENCE_RESPONSE_IDS\n     ), \"the OMN-15336 item-4 inference-response hold is not the expected id\"\n-    assert found[inference_response_end:] == FENCED_HOOK_EVENT_CAPTURE_IDS, (\n-        \"the OMN-16090 hook_event_capture hold is not the expected id\"\n+    hook_event_capture_end = inference_response_end + len(FENCED_HOOK_EVENT_CAPTURE_IDS)\n+    assert (\n+        found[inference_response_end:hook_event_capture_end]\n+        == FENCED_HOOK_EVENT_CAPTURE_IDS\n+    ), \"the OMN-16090 hook_event_capture hold is not the expected id\"\n+    assert found[hook_event_capture_end:] == FENCED_DELEGATION_UUID_CONVERSION_IDS, (\n+        \"the OMN-16493 delegation-0031 hold is not the expected id\"\n     )\n \n "}]}